# ── Output of generate_pages.py ──
# ~250 files: one index.html per post, member, publication and section, plus a
# redirect stub for every old-site URL. They are built in CI from the manifests
# and the index.html shell, so committing them would churn 250 files on every
# content edit and bury the one-line change that actually happened.
#
# index.html is NOT ignored — it is the template these are generated from. Nor
# is 404.html, which is hand-written.
news/*/index.html
news/index.html
people/*/index.html
people/index.html
# One page per photograph in the Memories tab. `people/*/index.html` above
# already covers people/memories/index.html itself; this is the level below it,
# and it is the only generated path on the site that is three segments deep.
people/memories/*/index.html
publications/*/index.html
publications/index.html
research/index.html
research/*/index.html

# `information/` is the one of these that is NOT purely generated: the tab
# modules (join.js, services.js and their -content.js) and the section's own
# img/ live beside the generated pages. A blanket `information/` here silently
# ignored three assets that were added after this rule — sussex-bg.jpg,
# sussex_landscape.jpg and logo_sussex.svg — so they were never committed, and
# the Contact and Services backdrops were 404s on the deployed site while
# working perfectly against a local server. Name the generated pages, never the
# folder.
information/index.html
information/*/index.html

# These six hold nothing but generated pages, so the folder is the rule —
# anchored with a leading slash, so `join/` cannot also swallow
# information/join/ and make it look as though the rule above were doing it.
/join/
/services/
/post/
/publication/
/authors/
/jobs/

# sitemap.xml and llms.txt are generated by the same script and are ignored for
# the same reason, which is worth spelling out because the instinct is to keep
# them: **the committed copies are never the ones served.** CI runs
# generate_pages.py before uploading, so both are overwritten on every deploy.
# Committing them bought nothing and cost 51 KB of diff on every content edit —
# which is the same churn the ~250 pages above are ignored to avoid, just
# concentrated into two files. Run the generator to see them.
sitemap.xml
llms.txt
# robots.txt joined them when its `Sitemap:` line stopped being a hand-kept
# fourth copy of the site's URL — see `_site_url` in generate_pages.py.
robots.txt

# ── Full-size sources for the derivatives ──
# Every one of these is the original a committed web copy was encoded from —
# keep them locally so a derivative can be regenerated, but they are megabytes
# each and no page ever requests them. See "The size budget" in CLAUDE.md.
*_full.jpg
*_full.png
*_full.webp
img/Intro.mp4

# ── Local noise ──
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
*.DS_Store
